          "en": "Supervised neutralisation calorimetry, an author-controlled adaptation of Göttingen's “Thermometrische Titration” (1333): 20.00 mL each supplied 0.200 mol/L HCl/NaOH, equal initial temperature, open insulated vessel, thermometer, stirring and goggles. C_cal is supplied or separately calibrated by water mixing. Blank: acid+water at equal volume. Synthetic calculation: m_solution=40.0 g, c_p=4.18 J/(g K), C_cal=20.0 J/K, ΔT=+1.20 K; task comparison value -57.0 kJ/mol H2O."
